This repository and its contents (including, without limitation, all
source code, documentation, and assets in `apps/`, `packages/`, `sdks/`,
`extensions/`, and `docs/`, except where a specific file, directory, or
package explicitly states otherwise) are proprietary and confidential.
No license, express or implied, to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
distribute, sublicense, or sell copies of this software is granted,
except under a separate written agreement with the copyright holder.

This file formalizes, as a single root-level notice, what every
package's own `package.json` already declares individually via
`"license": "UNLICENSED"` — this has been the project's consistent,
deliberate default since its first module. This file does not change
that policy; it makes it discoverable without having to check every
`package.json`.

## Exception

`packages/typescript-config` is licensed under the MIT License (see its
own `package.json`). It is trivial, non-proprietary `tsconfig.json`
boilerplate with no product logic, and licensing it permissively costs
nothing while simplifying reuse. This is the one intentional exception
to the default above, not an inconsistency to be "fixed."

## Third-party software

This project depends on numerous third-party open-source packages, each
under its own license (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, and others as declared
by each dependency). Using this software does not grant any rights to
those dependencies beyond what their own licenses already provide. See
`docs/security/supply-chain.md` for how third-party dependencies are
tracked, scanned, and updated.

---

Choosing whether to eventually open-source part or all of this project
under a specific OSS license (MIT, Apache-2.0, AGPL, or otherwise) is a
business decision for the project's owners to make deliberately, not one
made unilaterally by adding this file. This file only formalizes the
proprietary default that was already implied and consistently applied
across every package before it existed.
